<title>UK: Sun Life yr op companies pretax rises 3 pct.</title>
<headline>Sun Life yr op companies pretax rises 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 18.4		   vs n/a</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  *			vs *</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)  10.12		  vs n/a</p>
<p> Gp pretax profit	  156.4		  vs n/a</p>
<p> Turnover		    *			vs *</p>
<p> Op companies pretax     181.6		  vs 176.3</p>
<p>  Of which: Sun Life     110.3		  vs 89.4</p>
<p>		UAP Prov     63.2		   vs 64.2</p>
<p>		New Ireland  7.1		    vs 21.8</p>
<p>		Exeter Trust 1.0		    vs 0.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the British insurance group is Sun Life &amp; Provincial Holdings Plc. The results above are shown on a pro-forma basis and provide an indication of the holding company's results if the current structure had been in place in 1996. The company said changes in its composition and capital structure mean year-on-year comparisons are of limited value. Actual results are shown in the table below.  </p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 18.6		   vs 28.8</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)  6.78		   vs n/a</p>
<p> Gp pretax profit	  136.3		 vs 51.4</p>
<p> Op companies pretax     181.6		 vs 65.1</p>
<p>  Of which: Sun Life     110.3		 vs n/a</p>
<p>		UAP Prov     63.2		  vs 64.2</p>
<p>		New Ireland  7.1		   vs n/a</p>
<p>		Exeter Trust 1.0		   vs 0.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Sun Life and Provincial Holdings created a group last year including Sun Life, UAP Provincial and New Ireland. The company said it waws well placed for future growth.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
